  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd `research/p104-endpoint-rank-lean/` and its scoped workflow. This formalizes the written matrix implication in #2662 rather than proposing another construction.\n\n```text\nactual block-matrix product\n  rank B(product) <= sum of declared child charges\n  rank B(product)^p <= sum of charge^p, for 0 < p <= 1\n\nindependent binary source census\n  416 disjoint endpoint runs; rank mass 928\n```\n\nFive Lean theorem roots use only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`. The source census uses closed-form symplectic transvections and finite span sets, without importing predecessor executables. Its source-to-matrix binding remains Python evidence, not a kernel certificate.\n\nCredit commdata2338/#2662 for the endpoint-run theorem, rewrite class and histogram; ywz65/#2586 for the physical dual; #2497/#2551, Nick Petalas/#2550 and the retained native/compiler lineage. Exact heads, byte-identical source snapshots and full credit are in the package.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** #2662's matrix/concavity lower-bound implication is a written proof, with ranks checked by its retained native interpreter.\n  **After:** five kernel-checked roots, four altered formal contracts rejected, and all 416 binary run ranks independently reconstructed. This corroborates the existing 928 result; it does not claim a new numerical bound.\n- Six package test groups pass normally and optimized, including all 338 consumed frames, 230 small-frame cases, 256 binary matrix pairs, source/receipt corruption and a Git-free export. All 65 research-workflow tests pass. Ruff and YAML validation pass.\n- Linux x86_64, CPython 3.12.15, Lean 4.21.0, Mathlib `308445d7985027f538e281e18df29ca16ede2ba3`. Existing Mathlib build cache reused; no independent human review or hosted-CI success is claimed.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -Werror -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-endpoint-rank-lean\n# After fetching the pinned formal/lean Mathlib cache:\npython3.12 -Werror -B research/p104-endpoint-rank-lean/check_lean.py\n```\n\nStarted from canonical main `b5ea56e0a`, priority 5. Submission refresh at `a76748640` leaves guidance and all consumed inputs unchanged; a virtual merge is conflict-free. Final overlap covered 775 open PRs and 1,333 Discussion records with complete pagination, not arbitrary diffs or unpublished work. The existing investigation is [Discussion2619](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2619).\n\nPhysical/native identification, phases, hosting, idle/residual charges, rounded erasure, precision and all-size admission remain inherited or open. No native/selected cold replay, supplier admission or new kappa is claimed. The next scoped question is a kernel-checked canonical-frame and finite-rank binding.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\nOnly an opt-in package and scoped proof workflow are added. Selected records, frozen predecessors and production verifiers are unchanged.\n\n**Blast Radius:** research\n",
